      "value": "B-EM - BACnet Elevator Monitor"
    },
    "productDescription": {
      "provenance": "user-entered",
      "value": "A read-only BACnet/IP monitor for an elevator installation, built on the CAS BACnet Stack. It presents the series' three base sensor objects plus an Elevator Group / Lift / Escalator object family; the Lift follows a simulated lift car as it moves floor to floor. It answers ReadProperty and ReadPropertyMultiple, supports SubscribeCOV and SubscribeCOVPropertyMultiple (including the car's Car_Position, Car_Moving_Direction and Car_Door_Status), generates intrinsic event notifications (CHANGE_OF_STATE on the Lift's Passenger_Alarm, FAULT_LISTED on its Fault_Signals), accepts AcknowledgeAlarm, answers GetEventInformation, and handles DeviceCommunicationControl. It accepts WriteProperty only for Notification Class 1's Recipient_List (commissioning the alarm recipients), and no WritePropertyMultiple, Schedule, ReinitializeDevice or TimeSynchronization. It is a tutorial for implementers of the B-EM profile."
    },
    "productName": {
      "provenance": "user-entered",
      "value": "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-EM"
    },
